WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:03.942
Helena is the director.

2
00:00:03.942 --> 00:00:07.185
Her overview is the whole portfolio on one screen.

3
00:00:07.609 --> 00:00:11.961
Average progress against target, fourteen of thirty indicators on track,

4
00:00:11.961 --> 00:00:14.257
and the risks that are open right now.

5
00:00:14.694 --> 00:00:19.620
Programmes are listed worst first, so whatever needs her attention is at the top.

6
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.323
Only approved figures count.

7
00:00:21.759 --> 00:00:26.622
Coming up lists the reporting deadlines, and how many figures are approved for each.

8
00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:32.439
Programmes goes one level down: every project, with its timeline and budget spent.

9
00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:37.163
The on-track count is the same fourteen of thirty, counted the same way.

10
00:00:37.615 --> 00:00:42.330
The literacy project in Kurigram has spent sixty-four percent of its budget,

11
00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:45.121
and four of its five indicators are on track.

12
00:00:45.536 --> 00:00:48.142
Any indicator opens to its full history.

13
00:00:48.142 --> 00:00:51.140
Here is pupils attending the learning centres.

14
00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.707
The line is the actual, the dashes are the target.

15
00:00:54.707 --> 00:00:58.834
The third quarter figure was approved this week, and it is behind.

16
00:00:59.268 --> 00:01:01.162
Now the report for the funder.

17
00:01:01.162 --> 00:01:04.255
Reports are assembled from approved figures only.

18
00:01:04.683 --> 00:01:08.960
She picks a quarterly donor report, for the Learning and Skills programme.

19
00:01:10.929 --> 00:01:13.646
The last complete quarter is April to June.

20
00:01:13.646 --> 00:01:16.048
She names the report and assembles it.

21
00:01:21.226 --> 00:01:26.721
Everything is in one document: headline figures, each indicator against its target,

22
00:01:26.721 --> 00:01:30.296
what the teams wrote, activities delivered, and risks.

23
00:01:31.176 --> 00:01:33.350
She exports it as a PDF.

24
00:01:35.502 --> 00:01:39.773
The file is ready to attach to an email: a cover page and contents,

25
00:01:39.773 --> 00:01:42.132
then the figures, laid out for print.

26
00:01:43.581 --> 00:01:45.351
Some funders prefer a link.

27
00:01:45.351 --> 00:01:47.186
She creates a read-only one.

28
00:01:47.637 --> 00:01:52.576
The link opens this report, with its downloads, and nothing else in the workspace.

29
00:01:52.576 --> 00:01:54.021
Nobody needs an account.

30
00:01:54.472 --> 00:01:58.139
When the funder no longer needs it, she switches the link off.

31
00:01:58.139 --> 00:02:00.268
Anyone holding it then sees nothing.

32
00:02:00.714 --> 00:02:03.139
From the portfolio to a finished report,

33
00:02:03.139 --> 00:02:07.626
every number traces back to an approved figure and the evidence behind it.
